    <section class="steps">
        <h4 class="terms-tile">2. ENROLLMENT</h4>
        <p>This Enrollment Agreement (“Agreement”) is entered into as of the date when signed below, by and between _________ (“Student”) and _Hilbert College_ (“University”). Student is hereby enrolled into the program selected below (“Program”). The provisions, commitments, conditions, terms of use, and the privacy policy of this Agreement govern the Student’s enrollment in the Program selected, as offered by the University.</p>
        <p>Student will begin attending the Program with an expected start date of _________ and an expected completion date of __________.</p>
        <p>Student must make satisfactory academic progress toward completing his or her Program. To make satisfactory academic progress, Student must satisfy the academic criteria set forth below in this section. If Student is failing to make satisfactory academic progress in his or her Program at any evaluation time frame specified below, Student will be notified by the University of such failure and either be placed on academic probation or terminated from the Program as provided below.</p>
        <p>If Student falls one (1) week behind the Program schedule, Student will be placed on academic probation and would then receive individual remediation support from the University. Then, Student would remain on academic probation until he or she is caught back up with his or her original cohort.</p>
        <p>If Student subsequently falls two (2) weeks behind the Program schedule, Student will be terminated from the Program and Student’s access to the Program through the online platform will be revoked immediately.</p>
        <p>Further, if Student is placed on academic probation for four (4) consecutive weeks and has then failed to catch up with the Program schedule over the four (4) week period, Student will be terminated from the Program and their access to the Program through the online platform will be revoked immediately.</p>
        <p>If Student Is terminated from the Program due to his or her failure to maintain satisfactory academic progress, Student will be allowed the opportunity to repeat the Program if and when the Program is next offered. Any and all tuition and fees already paid by Student toward the cost of the Program will be credited to the Student’s account and will be applied toward the current cost of the new Program upon readmission.</p>
    </section>
