        <p>University reserves the right to change Program’s curriculum content and material in an effort to keep the curriculum current. No additional charges will be assessed to the Student for these types of Program changes and enhancements.</p>
        <p>University will provide access to an online platform, which will allow Student to attend online sessions, access digital learning materials, session recordings, assignments, and a learning plan, as applicable for the Program. Access to the online platform will only be available to the Student for the time period Student is attending the Program.</p>
        <p>Student must pay for, provide and maintain his or her own equipment and internet connectivity required to take and participate in the Program. The type of equipment and internet connectivity required for the Program includes: a desktop or laptop computer, a webcam, a headset with an echo cancellation mic, broadband internet connectivity with a minimum of 20MBPS, and an uninterrupted power supply. University is not responsible for any charges incurred for the acquisition of or usage of hardware or software, upgrades, or for installation, troubleshooting, or internet service provider fees.</p>
